-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Cybernoid II - The Revenge
  Publisher   Hewson Consultants, 1988
  Version     1.1

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Cybernoid II - The Revenge (1988)(Hewson Consultants)(128K).z80
  MD5         23f65550c22b654775a6f0dba9a76a4e

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    Armando Quaranta's Spec256 colours on the figures: the ship,
              enemies, weapons and effects in fuller colour over the game's
              own scenery, as approved for the earlier build. A painted set,
              colourist not named.

  Pace        original

  Changes     1.1: the 128K release with AY music; the original's pace kept by
              a limiter; works on NextZXOS v2.10; verified 128K cheats; the
              approved Enhanced colours unchanged

  Note        128K release with AY sound. Original colours with the clash
              removed by default; approved Enhanced colours optional and off
              by default. Known issues: none found in testing; two more tested
              cheats don't fit the loader's eight cheat lines. Missing:
              hardware testing, natural full-game completion, and the
              archive's cheat variants that don't apply to this release.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Infinite time
   3  Infinite weapons
   4  Immunity
   5  No guns
   6  No lifts
   7  No snakes
   8  No rockets
   9  No flying aliens
  10  No passage aliens

  The archive's POKEs, checked against this 128K release, using its own
  addresses for lives, time, weapons and immunity rather than the 48K ones.
  Two more tested cheats (No flying aliens, No passage aliens) are in the
  patch but beyond the loader's eight cheat lines.

